{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Compounder</b> — two times plene: מעשה רוקח (Exodus 30:25, \"the compounder's work\"); זבובי מות (Ecclesiastes 10:1) — ושמן רוקח (Ecclesiastes 10:1, \"and compounder's oil\"). This is what our Rabbis expounded: they would murmur about the incense, saying: by it Nadav and Avihu died; by it the assembly of Korah died, for \"death\" is written by רוקח, which is the incense. Moses said to them: see that the incense does not kill — on the contrary, it gives life, as it says: ויתן את הקטורת ויכפר על העם (Numbers 17:12, \"and he placed the incense and made atonement for the people\"), for it is written טהור קדש (pure, holy) — rather, the sin kills."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The phrase 'מות גבי רוקח' refers to the word מות appearing in the verse זבובי מות יביא יקר שמן רוקח (Ecclesiastes 10:1), where both מות and רוקח occur in the same verse, linking 'death' to the compounder's term."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:52.107576794Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}